WEBVTT

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:06.734
Captain's Log, Stardate 48693.2.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.968
We've altered course
to investigate

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.977
some unusually intense
photonic activity

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.979
in a nearby protostar.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.208
Lieutenant Torres and I
are beaming aboard samples

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.307
for further analysis.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.250
Containment field is active.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.583
We're ready for transport.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.883
Energize.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.220
That's strange.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.160
Both containers
should have been filled.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.689
Here's the problem.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.824
A slight breach
in the annular confinement beam.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.664
I'm aborting transport.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.727
Okay, let's try that again.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.329
Energizing.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.739
All right.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.972
I'll get a complete
phase spectrum analysis

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.502
on this as soon as possible.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.015
If this photonic matter
works as well as I think,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.447
it could boost the efficiency

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.145
of our power converters
15 percent.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.312
I'd say more like 20.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.845
How long will it take to finish
the preliminary analysis?

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.916
Um, six hours, maybe more.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.826
I'd like to get it
sooner than that.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.228
I believe Ensign Kim
is off duty.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.391
Could you use his help?

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.560
Can you convince him to
give up his free time?

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.364
I think I might be able to.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.495
Janeway to Kim.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.665
That's odd.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.503
Computer, locate Ensign Kim.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.975
Unable to comply.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.001
Ensign Kim
is not aboard the ship.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.279
Sensor logs show no record

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.409
of any unauthorized
transporter activity,

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.647
and all shuttlecraft
are accounted for.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:28.881
If Ensign Kim left the ship,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.981
he did not do so
by conventional means.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.515
His last shift ended
four hours ago,

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.891
and he was scheduled for time

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.555
on Holodeck 2
when he went off duty.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.824
No one has seen him since.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:38.888
Scan the holodeck.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.598
What's the matter?

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.832
There is significant
interference in the holodeck.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:49.341
I cannot obtain a clear scan.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.740
Is it a system malfunction?

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.574
I do not believe so.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.275
Commander.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.414
The holodeck
is definitely active.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.947
There appears to be
a program in progress.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.617
Can you shut it down?

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.185
The manual overrides
are not functioning.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.630
I cannot terminate the program.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.327
All right, let's go in.

00:04:40.411 --> 00:04:42.845
Computer, identify program.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.372
The program in progress
is a holonovel based

00:04:46.417 --> 00:04:48.385
on the epic Earth poem Beowulf.

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:50.216
Beowulf?

00:04:50.254 --> 00:04:54.384
An ancient English epic
set in sixth century Denmark,

00:04:54.425 --> 00:04:55.949
if I remember correctly.

00:04:55.994 --> 00:04:57.825
It's about a hero named Beowulf

00:04:57.862 --> 00:05:00.660
who fights a creature
that's terrorizing a kingdom

00:05:00.698 --> 00:05:02.393
and murdering its subjects.

00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:06.028
Monsters and swordplay,
that sort of thing.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.230
I'm not detecting
any life signs,

00:05:07.271 --> 00:05:09.637
but there is still
considerable interference.

00:05:09.674 --> 00:05:11.369
I can't determine the source.

00:05:12.977 --> 00:05:15.275
Speak as a friend

00:05:15.313 --> 00:05:17.679
or stand challenged.

00:05:17.715 --> 00:05:20.081
Computer, delete character.

00:05:23.988 --> 00:05:27.424
The holodeck command systems
must not be functioning either.

00:05:28.793 --> 00:05:31.557
We must also consider
the possibility

00:05:31.596 --> 00:05:34.064
that the safety programs
are malfunctioning as well.

00:05:34.098 --> 00:05:36.191
I'm am Freya, shield-maiden,

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:38.065
daughter of King Hrothgar.

00:05:38.102 --> 00:05:39.467
I hold this guard post

00:05:39.504 --> 00:05:42.268
against any intruders
who would bear us harm.

00:05:42.306 --> 00:05:43.705
So declare yourselves.

00:05:45.043 --> 00:05:46.510
I will hear your answer

00:05:46.544 --> 00:05:48.808
before you march any further
through this land.

00:05:48.846 --> 00:05:50.746
We have no desire to trespass.

00:05:50.782 --> 00:05:53.307
However, we are
on an urgent mission,

00:05:53.351 --> 00:05:54.750
so if you would allow us
to continue,

00:05:54.786 --> 00:05:55.980
we would appreciate it.

00:05:56.054 --> 00:05:57.988
What land do you call home?

00:05:58.022 --> 00:06:01.514
Your faces tell me
you are not men of the Danes.

00:06:01.559 --> 00:06:03.584
Are you...

00:06:03.628 --> 00:06:05.926
kinsmen of Beowulf?

00:06:07.799 --> 00:06:11.098
Yes.
We are Beowulf's kinsmen.

00:06:11.135 --> 00:06:13.729
My name is Chakotay,
and this is Tuvok.

00:06:13.771 --> 00:06:16.035
Have you seen Beowulf?

00:06:16.074 --> 00:06:18.565
Yes.

00:06:18.609 --> 00:06:20.600
He was like no other.

00:06:20.645 --> 00:06:25.548
Hair straight and raven black,
eyes bright with fierce fire,

00:06:25.583 --> 00:06:27.881
the burning gaze of a hero.

00:06:29.887 --> 00:06:31.787
Grandiloquence notwithstanding,

00:06:31.823 --> 00:06:34.223
that would qualify
as a description of Mr. Kim.

00:06:34.258 --> 00:06:36.385
How did you know he was Beowulf?

00:06:36.427 --> 00:06:38.327
This is Harry's holonovel.

00:06:38.362 --> 00:06:40.455
It'd make sense
that he'd be playing the hero.

00:06:40.498 --> 00:06:42.398
She might be able
to help us figure out

00:06:42.433 --> 00:06:43.491
what happened to him.

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:44.865
A reasonable assumption.

00:06:44.902 --> 00:06:47.564
Your kinsman was
a truly noble warrior.

00:06:47.605 --> 00:06:50.165
It is right you should
avenge his death.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.568
Yes, but first,

00:06:54.612 --> 00:06:58.104
we'd like to know more
about how Beowulf died.

00:06:58.149 --> 00:06:59.980
Of course.

00:07:00.084 --> 00:07:02.814
Come.
I will take you to the king.

00:07:05.089 --> 00:07:06.750
Hail, Lord Hrothgar.

00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:08.554
I bring new friends,

00:07:08.593 --> 00:07:11.118
Chakotay and Tuvok,
kinsmen of Beowulf,

00:07:11.162 --> 00:07:12.891
who come to avenge his death.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.899
Greet them well.

00:07:15.933 --> 00:07:18.766
I would bid you welcome
to my hall,

00:07:18.803 --> 00:07:22.398
but the days of glad tidings
are gone from this place.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.307
We grieve with you
for your kinsman.

00:07:25.343 --> 00:07:30.508
We had hoped that a warrior
of Beowulf's strength and renown

00:07:30.548 --> 00:07:33.984
would be able to deliver us
from our curse.

00:07:35.353 --> 00:07:38.345
Could you tell us exactly
what happened to him?

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:42.257
He met with the same fate
as did 30 of our own warriors.

00:07:42.293 --> 00:07:44.784
Grendel.

00:07:44.829 --> 00:07:46.888
That's the monster
who's been attacking you.

00:07:46.931 --> 00:07:49.559
Repelled by light and laughter,

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.727
the beast waits
until we slumber.

00:07:51.769 --> 00:07:53.964
Then, bereft of remorse,

00:07:54.005 --> 00:07:57.668
Grendel comes in murderous rage
to my hall

00:07:57.708 --> 00:07:59.539
to take my people,

00:07:59.577 --> 00:08:04.276
and there is nothing
anyone can do to stop it.

00:08:04.315 --> 00:08:07.011
If you are wise,

00:08:07.051 --> 00:08:10.851
you will forego your vengeance
and return home.

00:08:10.888 --> 00:08:13.914
Death lives here now.

00:08:13.991 --> 00:08:15.185
My Lord is fatigued.

00:08:15.226 --> 00:08:16.523
It is time to retire.

00:08:16.561 --> 00:08:19.530
We would like
more information about Beowulf.

00:08:19.564 --> 00:08:21.896
Would it be possible
to examine his body?

00:08:21.933 --> 00:08:24.595
The body of Beowulf is gone.

00:08:24.635 --> 00:08:27.399
Dragged down to Grendel's
foul lair, no doubt.

00:08:27.438 --> 00:08:29.167
The beast leaves no traces.

00:08:29.207 --> 00:08:31.038
Did anyone actually
see the battle?

00:08:31.075 --> 00:08:34.067
No. Beowulf chose
to face Grendel alone.

00:08:34.111 --> 00:08:37.877
Then I think we'd like to see
this Grendel for ourselves.

00:08:37.915 --> 00:08:39.382
To what purpose?

00:08:39.417 --> 00:08:42.545
To raise false hopes
in our king again

00:08:42.587 --> 00:08:44.145
as did your kinsman?

00:08:44.188 --> 00:08:46.679
Leave us alone in our misery.

00:08:46.724 --> 00:08:47.691
Unferth!

00:08:47.725 --> 00:08:48.919
These men are our guests.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.554
You will show them
the hospitality they deserve.

00:08:51.596 --> 00:08:53.188
They deserve nothing!

00:08:53.231 --> 00:08:56.860
If their Beowulf was truly
the champion he claimed to be,

00:08:56.901 --> 00:09:00.860
then Grendel would be dead,
his head mounted on a spear.

00:09:00.905 --> 00:09:04.636
Instead, we spend yet
another night in terror.

00:09:04.675 --> 00:09:06.199
If you would allow us

00:09:06.244 --> 00:09:09.304
to assist you, perhaps we could
help alleviate your terror.

00:09:10.882 --> 00:09:13.077
Your names mean nothing to me.

00:09:13.117 --> 00:09:15.381
There are no songs of your deeds

00:09:15.419 --> 00:09:18.445
nor stories of the battles
you have fought.

00:09:18.489 --> 00:09:20.787
Who are you to believe
you can slay Grendel?

00:09:20.825 --> 00:09:23.453
We have no intention
of slaying anyone.

00:09:23.494 --> 00:09:25.553
We simply wish to examine
the creature.

00:09:27.198 --> 00:09:30.725
Grendel might not wish
to be examined...

00:09:30.768 --> 00:09:32.895
without a fight.

00:09:32.937 --> 00:09:34.837
And if you would fight Grendel,

00:09:34.872 --> 00:09:37.807
then you will first
prove your worth to me.

00:09:38.809 --> 00:09:39.969
Defend yourselves.

00:09:42.146 --> 00:09:43.875
You are able warriors.

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:46.281
You may stand sentry tonight.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.252
You are brave men.

00:09:54.292 --> 00:09:57.318
I hope to see you again,
fate permitting.

00:10:03.301 --> 00:10:04.734
Chakotay to Janeway.

00:10:04.769 --> 00:10:05.929
Go ahead.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:09.167
Captain, we haven't found
any definite signs of Harry,

00:10:09.206 --> 00:10:11.697
but we've encountered
several holodeck characters

00:10:11.742 --> 00:10:13.471
who claim to know
what happened to him.

00:10:13.511 --> 00:10:17.311
Mr. Kim was running a holonovel
based on the poem Beowulf.

00:10:17.348 --> 00:10:19.748
According
to the holo-characters,

00:10:19.784 --> 00:10:21.945
he attempted to battle
a creature of some kind

00:10:21.986 --> 00:10:23.476
and was killed in the process.

00:10:24.689 --> 00:10:25.713
Killed?

00:10:25.756 --> 00:10:28.350
Since the safety programs
are malfunctioning,

00:10:28.392 --> 00:10:29.723
we must consider
the possibility.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.490
But...
you haven't found a body?

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:36.261
No. If we shut down the program,
we'd know if he's here or not.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.324
Run a diagnostic

00:10:37.368 --> 00:10:39.996
on the holodeck's
imaging control systems.

00:10:40.104 --> 00:10:42.402
If they're not working,
try to repair them.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.670
And relay your tricorder
scans to the Bridge.

00:10:44.709 --> 00:10:46.768
I'd like to analyze
your readings.

00:10:46.811 --> 00:10:49.405
Aye, Captain.
Chakotay out.

00:10:51.115 --> 00:10:53.606
The primary imaging matrix
should be here

00:10:53.651 --> 00:10:55.414
behind this wooden panel.

00:10:55.453 --> 00:10:58.513
I will attempt to locate
the auxiliary matrix.

00:11:00.825 --> 00:11:03.919
This ancient Earth culture
seems fascinated with monsters.

00:11:03.961 --> 00:11:06.521
Every culture has its demons.

00:11:06.564 --> 00:11:09.965
They embody the darkest emotions
of its people.

00:11:10.067 --> 00:11:12.865
Giving them physical form
in heroic literature

00:11:12.903 --> 00:11:15.701
is a way of exploring
those feelings.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:18.971
The Vok'sha of Rakella Prime

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:22.969
believe that hate is a beast
which lives inside the stomach.

00:11:23.047 --> 00:11:24.639
Their greatest mythical hero

00:11:24.682 --> 00:11:26.980
is a man who ate stones
for 23 days

00:11:27.051 --> 00:11:29.815
to kill the beast,
and became a saint.

00:11:29.854 --> 00:11:32.186
Such fables are necessary
only in cultures

00:11:32.223 --> 00:11:35.124
which unduly emphasize
emotional behavior.

00:11:35.159 --> 00:11:36.421
I would point out

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.621
there are no demons
in Vulcan literature.

00:11:38.662 --> 00:11:41.859
That might account
for its popularity.

00:11:41.899 --> 00:11:43.389
Bridge to Chakotay.

00:11:43.434 --> 00:11:45.595
Chakotay here.

00:11:45.636 --> 00:11:47.604
Commander, we've analyzed
your tricorder data.

00:11:47.638 --> 00:11:51.597
A deep-level scan shows minute
quantities of photonic energy.

00:11:51.642 --> 00:11:53.667
How could it be in the holodeck?

00:11:53.711 --> 00:11:56.009
We think it happened
when we beamed aboard

00:11:56.113 --> 00:11:57.705
the samples from the protostar.

00:11:57.748 --> 00:12:00.376
There was a breach in the
annular confinement beam,

00:12:00.418 --> 00:12:02.283
and photonic energy
must have leaked

00:12:02.319 --> 00:12:04.048
into the transporter system.

00:12:04.088 --> 00:12:06.147
And from there
into other ship systems as well.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:08.124
We've already found some
in the replicators.

00:12:08.159 --> 00:12:10.627
That raises an uncomfortable
possibility, Captain.

00:12:10.661 --> 00:12:12.959
If the holodeck's conversion
nodes were contaminated,

00:12:13.064 --> 00:12:15.294
Ensign Kim may have
inadvertently undergone

00:12:15.332 --> 00:12:16.959
the process
of matter conversion.

00:12:17.068 --> 00:12:20.504
You're saying he might have
been converted into energy?

00:12:20.538 --> 00:12:23.200
We have to consider it
a possibility.

00:12:26.077 --> 00:12:29.274
After all, the holodecks
are basically an outgrowth

00:12:29.313 --> 00:12:31.178
of transporter technology.

00:12:31.215 --> 00:12:34.207
Changing energy into matter
and back again.

00:12:34.251 --> 00:12:37.379
Every time a program is run.

00:12:37.421 --> 00:12:39.514
Except it's not supposed
to convert people.

00:12:39.557 --> 00:12:40.854
Hold on, Captain.

00:12:40.891 --> 00:12:42.085
Something's coming.

00:12:43.661 --> 00:12:45.993
It is an object approximately
one meter in diameter.

00:12:46.097 --> 00:12:48.827
I think Grendel
may be paying us a visit.

00:12:48.866 --> 00:12:50.834
Captain, the holo-characters
told us

00:12:50.868 --> 00:12:52.699
Kim was killed by Grendel.

00:12:52.736 --> 00:12:55.705
An examination of this part of
the program might be advisable.

00:12:55.739 --> 00:12:57.138
Proceed.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:03.268
Captain, I'm picking up signs
of matter/energy conversion.

00:13:03.314 --> 00:13:04.338
Emergency transport.

00:13:04.381 --> 00:13:05.871
Get them out of there now.

00:13:05.916 --> 00:13:07.816
I can't get a lock.

00:13:14.725 --> 00:13:16.522
Commander Chakotay, report.

00:13:17.695 --> 00:13:18.684
Mr. Tuvok?

00:13:18.729 --> 00:13:20.959
Captain, I've lost
their life signs.

00:13:21.065 --> 00:13:22.054
They're gone.

00:13:33.711 --> 00:13:35.679
This is a scan of the holodeck

00:13:35.713 --> 00:13:38.443
just before we lost contact
with Chakotay and Tuvok.

00:13:38.482 --> 00:13:40.416
The readings are pretty garbled,

00:13:40.451 --> 00:13:42.976
but I'm still inclined to think
that there is a malfunction

00:13:43.053 --> 00:13:45.453
in the holodeck's
matter conversion nodes.

00:13:45.489 --> 00:13:47.684
Photonic energy leaking
into the subsystems

00:13:47.725 --> 00:13:49.784
could certainly
damage the nodes,

00:13:49.827 --> 00:13:52.421
and it might have created
a defect in the program

00:13:52.463 --> 00:13:54.090
that occurs
when Grendel shows up.

00:13:54.131 --> 00:13:56.725
A defect that dematerialized
our people.

00:13:56.767 --> 00:13:58.598
I'm not willing
to accept the fact

00:13:58.636 --> 00:14:00.570
that Harry and the others
are gone for good.

00:14:01.572 --> 00:14:04.370
Their molecular patterns
might still be there.

00:14:04.408 --> 00:14:07.809
And if they are, we might be
able to rematerialize them.

00:14:07.845 --> 00:14:11.941
The only thing we can do is
go back into the holodeck.

00:14:11.982 --> 00:14:14.712
Study this... energy surge.

00:14:14.752 --> 00:14:15.912
Find out what exactly happened.

00:14:15.953 --> 00:14:17.079
Anyone who goes back in there

00:14:17.121 --> 00:14:18.520
might wind up
just like the others.

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:22.051
Maybe not anyone.

00:14:22.092 --> 00:14:23.150
Me?

00:14:23.194 --> 00:14:25.662
A hologram can't be
converted into energy.

00:14:25.696 --> 00:14:26.924
It already is energy.

00:14:26.964 --> 00:14:28.591
You're the perfect choice.

00:14:28.632 --> 00:14:31.965
How do you intend to transfer me
out of Sick Bay?

00:14:32.036 --> 00:14:33.970
We'll have to modify
your data stream protocols

00:14:34.038 --> 00:14:36.336
and imaging systems,
but the fact that you're going

00:14:36.373 --> 00:14:37.601
to the holodeck
simplifies things.

00:14:37.641 --> 00:14:40.201
The projection systems
are already in place there.

00:14:40.244 --> 00:14:41.871
And we're going
to give you complete control

00:14:41.912 --> 00:14:44.107
over your magnetic
containment field.

00:14:44.148 --> 00:14:45.979
You'll be able
to make yourself solid,

00:14:46.016 --> 00:14:47.881
or let matter pass
through you at will.

00:14:47.918 --> 00:14:49.977
Nothing on the holodeck
will be able to touch you...

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:51.419
unless you want it to.

00:14:54.325 --> 00:14:55.417
I see.

00:14:55.459 --> 00:14:57.326
Think of this as your first
away mission, Doctor.

00:14:57.326 --> 00:14:59.157
Think of this as your first
away mission, Doctor.

00:14:59.194 --> 00:15:01.492
I can understand
your hesitation,

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:03.896
but there are three
lives at stake,

00:15:03.932 --> 00:15:05.297
and you have the best chance

00:15:05.334 --> 00:15:07.165
of anyone on this ship
to save them.

00:15:09.004 --> 00:15:10.904
Do you understand that?

00:15:10.939 --> 00:15:12.497
Yes.

00:15:12.541 --> 00:15:14.406
Good.

00:15:14.443 --> 00:15:16.741
Your job is to find
the photonic energy surge

00:15:16.778 --> 00:15:17.938
and scan it closely.

00:15:17.979 --> 00:15:19.810
We need all the data we can get.

00:15:19.848 --> 00:15:21.145
You'll have to interact

00:15:21.183 --> 00:15:23.674
with the characters
in the holonovel,

00:15:23.719 --> 00:15:26.517
so make sure you're familiar
with the Beowulf story.

00:15:26.555 --> 00:15:30.355
Your circuit modifications
will be finished in three hours.

00:15:30.392 --> 00:15:32.758
Yes, Captain.

00:15:44.172 --> 00:15:48.666
Computer, access full text
of ancient Earth epic Beowulf

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:51.406
including historical annotation
and cultural references.

00:15:51.446 --> 00:15:54.540
Data compilation in progress.

00:15:54.583 --> 00:15:55.550
Doctor?

00:15:55.584 --> 00:15:57.449
Ah, Kes.
Come in.

00:15:57.486 --> 00:15:59.716
I don't know
how long I'll be gone,

00:15:59.755 --> 00:16:03.122
but my absence is no reason
to suspend your studies.

00:16:03.158 --> 00:16:05.524
How are you doing
with the protein synthesis text?

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.255
I finished it yesterday.

00:16:07.295 --> 00:16:08.785
Good. Then you may
as well start learning

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:10.263
how to operate
the base-pair sequencer.

00:16:10.298 --> 00:16:12.892
You'll find the manual
in the technical data base.

00:16:15.337 --> 00:16:16.929
Was there something else?

00:16:17.005 --> 00:16:18.438
There's something bothering you.

00:16:18.473 --> 00:16:19.633
Not at all.

00:16:19.674 --> 00:16:20.732
Now if you'll excuse me,

00:16:20.776 --> 00:16:22.573
I have a great deal
of preparation to do.

00:16:22.611 --> 00:16:24.772
You're nervous about
this mission, aren't you?

00:16:24.813 --> 00:16:26.110
Nervous?

00:16:28.016 --> 00:16:31.247
I can perform emergency surgery
without getting nervous.

00:16:31.286 --> 00:16:33.948
I can make life-or-death
decisions about patients

00:16:33.989 --> 00:16:35.513
without getting nervous.

00:16:35.557 --> 00:16:37.548
What makes you think
I'm nervous?

00:16:37.592 --> 00:16:39.753
Those things
are familiar to you.

00:16:39.795 --> 00:16:42.889
You've been programmed
to do them, but...

00:16:42.931 --> 00:16:48.836
this is different, isn't it?

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:58.809
I can describe every detail
of every piece of equipment

00:16:58.847 --> 00:17:01.839
in this Sick Bay... from bio-bed
to neurostimulator...

00:17:01.883 --> 00:17:09.312
but I've never even seen a sky
or a forest,

00:17:09.357 --> 00:17:13.123
let alone Vikings and monsters.

00:17:13.161 --> 00:17:17.029
I can't afford to fail.

00:17:17.065 --> 00:17:20.831
But I don't know what to expect
in that holodeck.

00:17:20.869 --> 00:17:22.302
You've been telling me that you

00:17:22.337 --> 00:17:24.897
deserve to be treated
like a member of the crew.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.931
Well, here's your chance.

00:17:27.008 --> 00:17:29.670
And I can tell you

00:17:29.711 --> 00:17:31.941
that none of the crew
knows exactly what to expect

00:17:32.047 --> 00:17:34.208
when they go on an away mission.

00:17:37.285 --> 00:17:41.119
Doctor, have you chosen
a name for yourself yet?

00:17:42.924 --> 00:17:45.950
I have narrowed the list
to three possibilities.

00:17:46.027 --> 00:17:49.087
Then let me suggest
you choose one before you go.

00:17:51.066 --> 00:17:54.126
It might help you feel more
like a Starfleet officer.

00:17:56.805 --> 00:17:58.670
Hmm.

00:17:58.707 --> 00:18:00.971
You may be right.

00:18:01.009 --> 00:18:02.567
I'll give it some thought.

00:18:03.812 --> 00:18:05.040
And Kes...

00:18:08.016 --> 00:18:09.916
thank you.

00:18:10.018 --> 00:18:12.043
Good luck.

00:18:20.729 --> 00:18:22.162
Paris to Janeway.

00:18:22.197 --> 00:18:23.755
We're ready
for the transfer, Captain.

00:18:23.798 --> 00:18:25.425
Good. Go ahead.

00:18:25.467 --> 00:18:27.458
How about you, Doctor?

00:18:27.502 --> 00:18:28.935
You ready?

00:18:29.004 --> 00:18:30.631
Of course.

00:18:30.672 --> 00:18:34.199
I've already transported
a tricorder onto the holodeck.

00:18:34.242 --> 00:18:37.939
Engaging transfer circuits...
now.

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:57.398
Is everything all right, Doctor?

00:18:57.432 --> 00:19:01.129
Yes. There were no problems
with the transfer.

00:19:01.169 --> 00:19:03.501
I'm on my way.

00:19:14.449 --> 00:19:16.314
Speak as a friend

00:19:16.351 --> 00:19:19.047
or stand challenged.

00:19:19.087 --> 00:19:20.054
I am...

00:19:20.088 --> 00:19:22.283
Yes, you're Freya,
the king's daughter.

00:19:22.324 --> 00:19:24.588
A female warrior
known as a shield-maiden.

00:19:24.626 --> 00:19:28.084
We have never met,
and yet you know my name?

00:19:28.129 --> 00:19:30.893
Are you a sorcerer?

00:19:30.932 --> 00:19:33.662
No.

00:19:33.702 --> 00:19:37.604
It's simply that...
your reputation precedes you.

00:19:37.639 --> 00:19:39.470
A warrior of your skill...

00:19:39.507 --> 00:19:42.169
you're quite famous
where I come from.

00:19:43.411 --> 00:19:45.845
I did not know
that word of my deeds

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:47.643
has carried to other lands.

00:19:47.682 --> 00:19:49.240
Tell me what you have heard.

00:19:50.518 --> 00:19:54.545
Well... your battle with...

00:19:54.589 --> 00:19:56.284
Scyld the Gar-Dane?

00:19:56.324 --> 00:19:57.450
...is practically legend.

00:19:57.492 --> 00:19:58.618
An incredible story.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.958
I burned his hall to the ground.

00:20:01.029 --> 00:20:03.327
There was nothing left
but ashes!

00:20:03.365 --> 00:20:04.491
Charming.

00:20:04.532 --> 00:20:05.624
And did you hear of my campaign

00:20:05.667 --> 00:20:07.396
against the heatho-bards
to the south?

00:20:07.435 --> 00:20:08.959
I fought them for...

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:10.799
I'd be delighted
to hear all about it,

00:20:10.839 --> 00:20:12.670
but I'm on an urgent
mission of my own.

00:20:12.707 --> 00:20:14.299
I'm looking for Grendel.

00:20:16.411 --> 00:20:19.574
Only a warrior would seek
that which others flee.

00:20:19.614 --> 00:20:21.172
What is your name?

00:20:21.216 --> 00:20:23.275
I'm glad you asked.

00:20:23.318 --> 00:20:25.809
My name is... Schweitzer.

00:20:25.854 --> 00:20:27.981
Dr. Schweitzer.

00:20:28.089 --> 00:20:29.852
"Schweitzer."

00:20:29.891 --> 00:20:33.850
A hero's name.

00:20:33.895 --> 00:20:36.363
Come, I will take you
to the king.

00:20:36.398 --> 00:20:37.422
Hmm.

00:20:38.466 --> 00:20:41.458
The hall is not far from here.

00:20:43.805 --> 00:20:47.605
Look... fortune is with us.

00:20:47.642 --> 00:20:50.873
Atuta... a most powerful plant.

00:20:50.912 --> 00:20:52.903
What exactly do you
intend to do with it?

00:20:52.947 --> 00:20:56.007
We brew the atuta into a broth,
which we drink before battle.

00:20:56.051 --> 00:20:57.848
It brings on
the spirit of the bear,

00:20:57.886 --> 00:21:00.821
and gives us strength
to swing our swords.

00:21:00.855 --> 00:21:02.755
It's more likely to bring on
profuse sweating,

00:21:02.791 --> 00:21:04.725
convulsions, and acute delirium.

00:21:04.759 --> 00:21:07.227
This is an Amanita muscaria...

00:21:07.262 --> 00:21:09.127
a fungus common
to subartic climates,

00:21:09.164 --> 00:21:11.223
and, let me assure you,
quite poisonous.

00:21:11.266 --> 00:21:14.667
Yes, but those it does not kill,
it makes strong.

00:21:14.703 --> 00:21:16.728
A most hearty plant.

00:21:16.771 --> 00:21:18.762
Are you a master of herb-lore?

00:21:18.807 --> 00:21:21.105
Well, in a way, I suppose I am.

00:21:21.142 --> 00:21:24.839
You are truly a man of many
talents, Lord Schweitzer.

00:21:24.879 --> 00:21:26.972
Your people must
value you greatly.

00:21:27.082 --> 00:21:29.073
You would think so.

00:21:31.119 --> 00:21:33.087
Hail, Lord Hrothgar!

00:21:33.121 --> 00:21:35.646
I bring a new friend,
Schweitzer,

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.419
who has come to destroy Grendel.

00:21:37.459 --> 00:21:39.950
Greet him well.

00:21:39.994 --> 00:21:42.861
I would bid you welcome
to my hall,

00:21:42.897 --> 00:21:47.129
but the days of glad tidings
are gone from this place.

00:21:47.168 --> 00:21:49.693
I'm sorry to hear that,

00:21:49.738 --> 00:21:51.501
but with your permission,
sir, I'd like to stay

00:21:51.539 --> 00:21:53.336
here tonight,
and wait for Grendel.

00:21:53.374 --> 00:21:55.274
To what purpose?

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:58.768
To raise false hopes again,

00:21:58.813 --> 00:22:01.043
as have others before you?

00:22:01.082 --> 00:22:03.880
Leave us alone in our misery.

00:22:03.918 --> 00:22:06.148
I'm afraid I can't do that.

00:22:06.187 --> 00:22:07.677
I have a mission.

00:22:07.722 --> 00:22:09.952
Your name means nothing to me.

00:22:09.991 --> 00:22:12.459
There are no songs
of your deeds

00:22:12.494 --> 00:22:15.486
nor stories of the battles
you have fought.

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:18.465
Who are you to believe
you can slay Grendel?

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:21.697
I'm simply a... warrior.

00:22:21.736 --> 00:22:23.567
I'm only concerned with Grendel.

00:22:23.605 --> 00:22:25.129
I have no quarrel with you.

00:22:25.173 --> 00:22:26.367
Indeed you do,

00:22:26.407 --> 00:22:28.466
and if you will fight Grendel,

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:33.447
then you will first
prove your worth to me.

00:22:33.481 --> 00:22:36.507
Defend yourself!

00:22:42.957 --> 00:22:44.049
Fate be with you.

00:22:54.636 --> 00:22:58.265
If this is your best,
then you should thank me.

00:22:58.306 --> 00:23:01.935
Grendel would destroy you
with far greater ease than I.

00:23:03.311 --> 00:23:05.142
This is absurd.

00:23:10.385 --> 00:23:11.682
So be it.

00:23:18.159 --> 00:23:19.956
You might want to put
some ice on that.

00:23:20.028 --> 00:23:21.427
It'll take down the swelling.

00:23:22.564 --> 00:23:24.964
Our time of deliverance
is at hand.

00:23:25.033 --> 00:23:28.059
We have been given
a new champion...

00:23:28.102 --> 00:23:30.366
one whom weapons cannot hurt.

00:23:30.405 --> 00:23:32.464
The one who will destroy Grendel

00:23:32.507 --> 00:23:33.940
and end our suffering.

00:23:33.975 --> 00:23:36.239
All hail the hero!

00:23:36.277 --> 00:23:39.906
- All hail Schweitzer!
- All hail Schweitzer!

00:23:39.948 --> 00:23:42.576
Schweitzer! Schweitzer!

00:23:42.617 --> 00:23:44.744
Schweitzer!
Schweitzer!

00:23:44.786 --> 00:23:46.720
Schweitzer! Schweitzer!

00:23:46.754 --> 00:23:48.847
Schweitzer!
Schweitzer!

00:23:48.890 --> 00:23:50.881
Schweitzer! Schweitzer!

00:23:50.925 --> 00:23:52.415
Schweitzer!
Schweitzer!

00:23:57.232 --> 00:23:59.564
Eat, eat.

00:23:59.601 --> 00:24:01.330
What is it?

00:24:01.369 --> 00:24:02.563
Elk.

00:24:02.604 --> 00:24:06.233
When I built this hall,
the forest ran thick with them,

00:24:06.274 --> 00:24:09.937
but today, game's more scarce.

00:24:09.978 --> 00:24:11.411
Enjoy it, Lord Schweitzer.

00:24:11.446 --> 00:24:13.971
It is a great delicacy
in our land.

00:24:25.393 --> 00:24:28.055
Hmm. It's quite good.

00:24:28.096 --> 00:24:31.588
We rarely hear stories
of other lands.

00:24:31.633 --> 00:24:34.534
Honor us with
a tale of your home

00:24:34.569 --> 00:24:36.196
to gladden our hearts.

00:24:36.237 --> 00:24:38.501
I'm not much of a storyteller.

00:24:38.539 --> 00:24:40.507
Please...

00:24:40.541 --> 00:24:41.633
indulge us.

00:24:41.676 --> 00:24:44.804
Yes, tell us a tale
of your prowess in battle.

00:24:44.846 --> 00:24:48.282
Well, there was the time

00:24:48.316 --> 00:24:50.648
I managed to stop the spread
of Parinisti measles

00:24:50.685 --> 00:24:52.778
before it became epidemic.

00:24:52.820 --> 00:24:55.380
For a while,
things were touch and go.

00:24:55.423 --> 00:24:57.857
Six people came down with it.

00:24:57.892 --> 00:24:59.189
Fortunately, I was able

00:24:59.227 --> 00:25:02.128
to isolate the endoplasmic virus
and replicate it

00:25:02.163 --> 00:25:03.926
in order to form an antibody.

00:25:03.998 --> 00:25:07.331
Even then, it wasn't altogether

00:25:07.368 --> 00:25:10.437
clear I could create
an effective vaccine.

00:25:10.570 --> 00:25:13.937
But I worked at it
for 74 hours straight,

00:25:13.973 --> 00:25:16.134
and managed to create
an inoculation

00:25:16.176 --> 00:25:17.404
that successfully protected
the crew.

00:25:17.444 --> 00:25:19.344
You'll excuse me, my Lord,

00:25:19.379 --> 00:25:22.644
if I take leave of this...
folly.

00:25:24.951 --> 00:25:27.419
A truly unique tale.

00:25:27.454 --> 00:25:29.354
Come, Lord Schweitzer.

00:25:29.389 --> 00:25:31.550
Allow me to show you my home.

00:25:33.026 --> 00:25:37.486
If you are in need of anything,
please do not hesitate to ask.

00:25:37.530 --> 00:25:39.327
All I need is to find Grendel.

00:25:39.365 --> 00:25:42.562
You are a true champion...
always ready for the fight.

00:25:42.602 --> 00:25:44.297
Ah, perhaps you
would like some mead

00:25:44.337 --> 00:25:45.804
to fortify yourself for battle?

00:25:45.839 --> 00:25:47.568
No, thank you.
I'm fine.

00:25:47.607 --> 00:25:50.576
Away. You're disturbing
Lord Schweitzer!

00:25:50.610 --> 00:25:56.071
It was with that weapon
I made my first kill.

00:25:56.115 --> 00:25:58.106
I was 11 years old.

00:25:58.151 --> 00:26:01.712
You killed someone
when you were 11?

00:26:01.754 --> 00:26:04.120
Well, it's a poor weapon,
I agree,

00:26:04.157 --> 00:26:05.886
but a token of my youth.

00:26:05.925 --> 00:26:08.689
You must have similar trophies
from your own childhood.

00:26:09.996 --> 00:26:14.365
I... don't remember much
about my childhood.

00:26:14.400 --> 00:26:15.594
Well, I am certain

00:26:15.635 --> 00:26:18.160
you distinguished yourself
in battle many times

00:26:18.204 --> 00:26:19.796
and did honor to your father.

00:26:19.839 --> 00:26:22.865
My Lord, it grows late.

00:26:22.909 --> 00:26:24.843
It is time to retire.

00:26:24.878 --> 00:26:27.438
Always with you
it is time to sleep.

00:26:27.480 --> 00:26:29.243
Perhaps you have forgotten

00:26:29.282 --> 00:26:32.513
that the work of a warrior
is battle, not rest!

00:26:32.552 --> 00:26:35.180
You would do well to learn
from Lord Schweitzer.

00:26:37.957 --> 00:26:40.323
This was
a beautiful hall once...

00:26:40.360 --> 00:26:42.328
before Grendel.

00:26:42.362 --> 00:26:45.490
You will make it so again.

00:26:45.532 --> 00:26:48.501
You have our thanks.

00:26:49.702 --> 00:26:52.034
I appreciate your faith
in me, Sire.

00:26:57.176 --> 00:26:58.666
Come, my lord.

00:26:59.979 --> 00:27:03.005
You may have deceived
them with your tricks,

00:27:05.018 --> 00:27:08.419
but the king is old
and desperate for hope,

00:27:08.454 --> 00:27:10.354
and the rest are just fools!

00:27:10.390 --> 00:27:13.052
You have nothing
to worry about, Unferth.

00:27:13.092 --> 00:27:15.253
Once I'm done with Grendel,
I'll be leaving.

00:27:15.295 --> 00:27:16.785
We shall see.

00:27:16.829 --> 00:27:18.558
The morning will prove

00:27:18.598 --> 00:27:21.658
if your deeds are
as strong as your words.

00:27:30.610 --> 00:27:33.408
The nights here are cold.

00:27:33.446 --> 00:27:35.914
I wanted to make certain
you were comfortable.

00:27:35.949 --> 00:27:38.782
I appreciate your concern.

00:27:44.357 --> 00:27:47.019
I thought everyone
had gone to sleep.

00:27:49.329 --> 00:27:54.665
Sleep does not come
easily in this place.

00:27:54.701 --> 00:27:57.295
Not anymore.

00:27:58.972 --> 00:28:01.805
I was taught the world
would end in winter.

00:28:01.841 --> 00:28:04.810
First, there would
be a desperate cold,

00:28:04.844 --> 00:28:08.143
followed by a demon who
would devour the sun.

00:28:09.649 --> 00:28:13.312
It has been long
since we felt summer,

00:28:13.353 --> 00:28:16.083
and a demon does walk
these halls.

00:28:18.558 --> 00:28:19.923
Freya...

00:28:19.959 --> 00:28:22.484
your world
isn't coming to an end.

00:28:22.528 --> 00:28:24.496
Perhaps not,

00:28:24.530 --> 00:28:27.021
but it has changed.

00:28:27.066 --> 00:28:30.399
Every night the monster comes,

00:28:30.436 --> 00:28:32.597
and every day
our numbers are lessened,

00:28:32.639 --> 00:28:34.197
and no one will speak of it.

00:28:34.240 --> 00:28:37.141
No one speaks of the fear
that he will be next.

00:28:37.176 --> 00:28:41.510
But each meal becomes
quieter than the last,

00:28:41.547 --> 00:28:45.483
and after a time,
we barely speak at all.

00:28:45.518 --> 00:28:49.545
Do you know what it is
to be alone among many,

00:28:49.589 --> 00:28:51.955
and unable to speak your fears?

00:28:54.127 --> 00:28:56.357
I think I do.

00:28:56.396 --> 00:28:58.762
How do you survive?

00:28:58.798 --> 00:29:01.494
I'm still learning how.

00:29:02.902 --> 00:29:05.632
I'm sure
that's not very helpful.

00:29:07.373 --> 00:29:09.034
Sometimes I believe

00:29:09.075 --> 00:29:12.272
I can see the moment
of my own death.

00:29:12.311 --> 00:29:15.906
It comes in battle, I think,

00:29:15.982 --> 00:29:19.281
my sword raised high.

00:29:21.354 --> 00:29:25.313
It is said that fate
often spares a doomed warrior,

00:29:25.358 --> 00:29:27.519
if his courage can prevail.

00:29:27.560 --> 00:29:30.825
But there have been days

00:29:30.863 --> 00:29:33.093
when I felt my own courage
falter...

00:29:33.132 --> 00:29:35.692
and then you came.

00:29:35.735 --> 00:29:38.636
I'm glad I could help.

00:29:38.671 --> 00:29:40.571
Perhaps I can help you.

00:29:42.608 --> 00:29:47.841
Before combat, it is most
important to stay warm.

00:29:48.881 --> 00:29:50.678
Well, you've done
an excellent job

00:29:50.717 --> 00:29:52.412
with the fire, I'm sure I'll...

00:30:04.163 --> 00:30:08.259
Fire is not the only heat,
Lord Schweitzer.

00:30:08.301 --> 00:30:11.293
You know where I sleep.

00:30:33.926 --> 00:30:35.587
Holodeck to Bridge.

00:30:35.628 --> 00:30:37.118
We're monitoring you.

00:30:37.163 --> 00:30:41.429
Captain, I'm picking up
readings of photonic energy.

00:30:47.073 --> 00:30:48.472
Captain, it's right
in front of me.

00:30:48.508 --> 00:30:52.501
It's some kind of...
photonic energy formation.

00:30:57.083 --> 00:30:58.277
Emergency!

00:30:58.317 --> 00:30:59.545
Get me out of here!

00:30:59.585 --> 00:31:00.745
Now!

00:31:00.787 --> 00:31:03.119
Sick Bay, emergency transfer.

00:31:03.156 --> 00:31:04.817
I'm on it.

00:31:10.863 --> 00:31:12.160
Sick Bay, report.

00:31:12.198 --> 00:31:15.793
Uh... I have him, Captain...

00:31:15.835 --> 00:31:17.063
more or less.

00:31:18.838 --> 00:31:21.272
I think you better come
take a look at this.

00:31:39.659 --> 00:31:41.490
How does it feel?

00:31:41.527 --> 00:31:43.085
Just like the old one, actually.

00:31:43.129 --> 00:31:45.222
Apparently, contact
with photonic energy

00:31:45.264 --> 00:31:47.198
disrupted
your magnetic cohesion,

00:31:47.233 --> 00:31:48.200
but we're still not sure

00:31:48.234 --> 00:31:49.565
if that's what happened
to the others.

00:31:49.602 --> 00:31:51.797
Captain, take a look at this.

00:31:51.838 --> 00:31:53.635
The readings
from the Doctor's tricorder

00:31:53.673 --> 00:31:56.767
when the energy surge
made contact with him.

00:31:56.809 --> 00:31:59.676
They're showing
a synaptic pattern.

00:31:59.712 --> 00:32:01.009
I wouldn't expect to see

00:32:01.047 --> 00:32:03.038
something like this
in photonic energy.

00:32:03.082 --> 00:32:04.310
Is this the first time

00:32:04.350 --> 00:32:05.942
those patterns
have shown up like this?

00:32:06.018 --> 00:32:07.144
Yes, but it's the first time

00:32:07.186 --> 00:32:09.950
we've had clear readings
from a moment of contact.

00:32:10.022 --> 00:32:13.924
I wonder if I could produce
these same patterns

00:32:13.960 --> 00:32:15.655
in the samples
we have in Engineering.

00:32:15.695 --> 00:32:16.957
If you can, you might be able

00:32:16.996 --> 00:32:19.590
to get more information
about how photonic energy

00:32:19.632 --> 00:32:20.860
damaged the holodeck systems.

00:32:20.900 --> 00:32:22.128
I'm on it.

00:32:22.168 --> 00:32:23.533
I'll give you a hand.

00:32:27.640 --> 00:32:29.335
Okay...

00:32:29.375 --> 00:32:31.639
I've initiated
a polarization field.

00:32:31.677 --> 00:32:33.975
I'm introducing it
into the container.

00:32:34.046 --> 00:32:35.707
We're getting a reaction.

00:32:35.748 --> 00:32:38.774
It's producing a synaptic
pattern all right...

00:32:38.818 --> 00:32:40.752
highly complex.

00:32:41.787 --> 00:32:42.776
What's that?

00:32:46.959 --> 00:32:49.427
Whatever it is, it's cutting
through the bulkheads.

00:32:49.462 --> 00:32:50.986
Let's get a containment field
around it.

00:32:51.030 --> 00:32:53.328
It's heading
for Deck 14, Section C-5.

00:32:53.366 --> 00:32:55.891
Okay, now I've got
a containment field blocking it.

00:32:57.036 --> 00:32:59.766
Whoa.
It's changing direction.

00:32:59.805 --> 00:33:01.932
It's like it's avoiding
the containment field.

00:33:02.041 --> 00:33:03.633
Let's give it another try.

00:33:03.676 --> 00:33:06.236
Now it's blocked on three sides.

00:33:06.279 --> 00:33:07.610
It's changing course.

00:33:07.647 --> 00:33:08.875
Heading for the open side.

00:33:11.884 --> 00:33:14.114
Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?

00:33:14.153 --> 00:33:15.916
Those synaptic patterns...

00:33:15.955 --> 00:33:19.288
could be some sort
of neural net.

00:33:19.325 --> 00:33:21.953
We may be dealing
with a life-form.

00:33:21.994 --> 00:33:23.484
Bridge to Engineering.

00:33:23.529 --> 00:33:24.757
Torres here.

00:33:24.797 --> 00:33:27.789
We're detecting an energy mass
moving through the ship.

00:33:27.833 --> 00:33:30.529
Right. It broke through
the sample container.

00:33:30.569 --> 00:33:33.970
Captain, it's showing
the properties of a life-form.

00:33:34.040 --> 00:33:36.508
A life-form?

00:33:36.542 --> 00:33:38.271
It seems to have a neural net,

00:33:38.311 --> 00:33:40.871
and it's demonstrating
signs of intelligent behavior.

00:33:40.913 --> 00:33:42.574
It's cutting it's way
through the ship.

00:33:42.615 --> 00:33:44.139
Heading for the outer hull.

00:33:44.183 --> 00:33:46.310
It'll breach
in about 15 seconds.

00:33:46.352 --> 00:33:48.320
Are there any critical systems
in its path?

00:33:48.354 --> 00:33:49.321
Negative.

00:33:49.355 --> 00:33:50.515
Then let it go.

00:33:50.556 --> 00:33:52.888
Be ready to seal the hull breach
with a force field.

00:33:52.925 --> 00:33:55.985
I'll have a damage control team
standing by for repairs.

00:33:56.028 --> 00:33:58.155
And let's track it on sensors
when it gets out.

00:33:58.197 --> 00:34:00.597
Captain,
it's penetrating the outer hull.

00:34:00.633 --> 00:34:02.931
Force field is in place.

00:34:03.002 --> 00:34:06.438
I'm showing the energy form
100 meters off our port side.

00:34:06.472 --> 00:34:08.531
Let's get it on screen.

00:34:15.381 --> 00:34:17.872
What was that?

00:34:24.156 --> 00:34:27.148
It appears to be some kind
of photonic lattice.

00:34:27.193 --> 00:34:29.423
And it seems pretty clear
that the energy form

00:34:29.462 --> 00:34:31.123
was trying to get back to it.

00:34:31.163 --> 00:34:34.724
As though it's...
a shelter of some kind.

00:34:34.767 --> 00:34:36.962
Or maybe
a transportation device...

00:34:37.069 --> 00:34:39.469
their equivalent of a ship.

00:34:39.505 --> 00:34:42.565
At any rate,
we had sensor contact

00:34:42.608 --> 00:34:45.168
for a few seconds,
and we picked up

00:34:45.211 --> 00:34:48.977
three distinct bioelectrical
patterns inside it.

00:34:49.015 --> 00:34:50.175
Bioelectrical?

00:34:50.216 --> 00:34:52.150
What are you suggesting,
Captain?

00:34:52.184 --> 00:34:54.311
We have three missing crewmen.

00:34:54.353 --> 00:34:55.980
Our best guess has been

00:34:56.088 --> 00:34:57.919
that they were somehow
converted into energy

00:34:57.957 --> 00:34:59.322
while they were on the holodeck.

00:34:59.358 --> 00:35:01.622
We find no sign of them
on this ship.

00:35:01.660 --> 00:35:05.289
Then we pick up three discrete
patterns in that lattice,

00:35:05.331 --> 00:35:08.027
three patterns that don't match
anything else in the lattice

00:35:08.067 --> 00:35:10.900
and which have
biological components.

00:35:10.936 --> 00:35:13.700
I don't think it's a stretch
to hypothesize

00:35:13.739 --> 00:35:15.138
that those are our crew members,

00:35:15.174 --> 00:35:18.876
converted into a kind
of photonic energy.

00:35:19.009 --> 00:35:20.943
But what are they
doing over there?

00:35:21.011 --> 00:35:22.478
How did they get there?

00:35:22.512 --> 00:35:23.945
We have good evidence now

00:35:24.014 --> 00:35:27.950
that there are photonic beings
that live in that protostar...

00:35:27.985 --> 00:35:30.385
life-forms
that have intelligence.

00:35:30.420 --> 00:35:31.682
We didn't know that

00:35:31.722 --> 00:35:34.156
when we beamed those
energy samples on board.

00:35:34.191 --> 00:35:36.352
We had no idea
that what we were doing,

00:35:36.393 --> 00:35:39.954
in essence, was capturing
those life-forms.

00:35:40.063 --> 00:35:42.156
We locked them
in a containment field,

00:35:42.199 --> 00:35:44.759
and began to experiment on them.

00:35:44.801 --> 00:35:46.996
If my people were
taken like that...

00:35:48.739 --> 00:35:51.105
I know
what my response would be.

00:35:51.141 --> 00:35:54.304
I would do whatever was
necessary to get them back.

00:35:54.344 --> 00:35:56.471
Then you think
they have simply...

00:35:56.513 --> 00:35:57.946
retaliated against us?

00:35:57.981 --> 00:35:59.539
Yes.

00:35:59.583 --> 00:36:03.485
These beings can manifest
themselves on the holodeck

00:36:03.520 --> 00:36:05.579
in the matrix
of a holo-character.

00:36:05.622 --> 00:36:06.919
That's how they were able
to take

00:36:07.024 --> 00:36:09.185
our crew members hostage.

00:36:09.226 --> 00:36:10.818
Captain, if you're
right about this,

00:36:10.861 --> 00:36:13.455
then we should return
the remaining life-form.

00:36:13.497 --> 00:36:16.364
A gesture...
to show we mean well.

00:36:16.400 --> 00:36:17.924
It's certainly worth a try.

00:36:18.001 --> 00:36:20.663
If I took the life-form
onto the holodeck

00:36:20.704 --> 00:36:22.934
and release it to Grendel,

00:36:22.973 --> 00:36:25.305
maybe they'll understand
and release our people.

00:36:25.342 --> 00:36:28.470
Ordinarily, officers go
through intensive training

00:36:28.512 --> 00:36:29.672
before they're put

00:36:29.713 --> 00:36:32.307
into a First Contact
situation...

00:36:32.349 --> 00:36:35.614
but you're the only one
who can do this safely.

00:36:35.652 --> 00:36:37.950
I'd like to finish
what I started, Captain.

00:36:38.055 --> 00:36:39.352
I can do this.

00:36:39.389 --> 00:36:41.323
I agree.

00:36:41.358 --> 00:36:43.758
Make arrangements
to transfer the life-form

00:36:43.794 --> 00:36:47.161
to a container,
so the Doctor can carry it.

00:36:49.166 --> 00:36:51.134
But, remember...

00:36:51.168 --> 00:36:53.466
if you're holding the container,

00:36:53.503 --> 00:36:56.131
you'll have to stay
in solid form.

00:36:56.173 --> 00:36:58.971
I understand.

00:37:02.779 --> 00:37:04.144
Freya?

00:37:06.850 --> 00:37:08.078
Freya!

00:37:13.890 --> 00:37:16.051
Lord Schweitzer!

00:37:16.093 --> 00:37:19.028
We thought the Grendel
had taken you.

00:37:19.062 --> 00:37:21.292
Not... entirely.

00:37:21.331 --> 00:37:24.095
How did you survive?

00:37:24.134 --> 00:37:26.932
That would be difficult
to explain,

00:37:26.970 --> 00:37:30.269
but that's not
important right now.

00:37:30.307 --> 00:37:33.936
This is a talisman
to destroy Grendel...

00:37:34.044 --> 00:37:35.568
You lie!

00:37:35.612 --> 00:37:38.206
No man could survive
an encounter with Grendel

00:37:38.248 --> 00:37:40.739
unless he were
in league with the beast.

00:37:40.784 --> 00:37:44.652
You have brought that talisman
to destroy us all.

00:37:44.688 --> 00:37:45.655
That is not true.

00:37:45.689 --> 00:37:47.156
He has returned to help us.

00:37:47.190 --> 00:37:48.282
No!

00:37:48.325 --> 00:37:51.385
You speak his lies now.

00:37:51.428 --> 00:37:52.895
He has bewitched you.

00:37:52.929 --> 00:37:57.491
Unferth, I need to get
this talisman to the hall.

00:37:57.534 --> 00:37:59.229
Then that gives me reason enough

00:37:59.269 --> 00:38:02.238
to make sure
it never gets there.

00:38:10.714 --> 00:38:11.840
No! Please!

00:38:11.882 --> 00:38:13.850
You don't know
what you're doing.

00:38:27.230 --> 00:38:29.630
Prepare to die, demon.

00:38:40.043 --> 00:38:41.704
Freya...

00:38:45.649 --> 00:38:47.310
My Lord...

00:38:49.986 --> 00:38:51.749
my time has come.

00:38:51.788 --> 00:38:53.551
Freya, I'm sorry.

00:38:56.126 --> 00:38:57.718
There's nothing I can do.

00:38:57.761 --> 00:39:01.253
It is a good death.

00:39:03.667 --> 00:39:05.498
Take my sword.

00:39:05.535 --> 00:39:08.800
Stop Unferth and Grendel.

00:39:10.707 --> 00:39:12.470
I won't forget you.

00:39:13.810 --> 00:39:16.472
Then I die happily...

00:39:16.513 --> 00:39:20.677
with your name on my lips.

00:39:20.717 --> 00:39:24.517
Farewell...

00:39:24.554 --> 00:39:26.715
Schweitzer.

00:39:50.847 --> 00:39:52.872
Here, Sire.

00:39:58.088 --> 00:39:59.146
My Lord...

00:39:59.189 --> 00:40:01.953
you know me as a true warrior.

00:40:01.992 --> 00:40:03.619
You know I am
the one hope you have

00:40:03.660 --> 00:40:05.150
to rid your kingdom of Grendel.

00:40:05.195 --> 00:40:08.323
That talisman will aid me
in my conquest.

00:40:08.365 --> 00:40:09.662
I must have it.

00:40:09.699 --> 00:40:11.428
Do not listen to him.

00:40:11.468 --> 00:40:14.494
He has already killed Freya.

00:40:32.856 --> 00:40:34.721
Stop him, my Lord!

00:40:34.758 --> 00:40:36.817
He is a madman!

00:40:36.860 --> 00:40:39.658
The only reason you won't die

00:40:39.696 --> 00:40:44.258
is that I've taken an oath
to do no harm.

00:41:02.352 --> 00:41:04.183
Grendel...

00:41:04.221 --> 00:41:05.620
I'm ready for you.

00:41:19.669 --> 00:41:22.604
I don't know if you
can understand me...

00:41:22.639 --> 00:41:24.971
but watch.

00:41:25.075 --> 00:41:27.134
I'm setting this one free.

00:41:37.354 --> 00:41:40.482
There's no need
for any more of this.

00:41:40.523 --> 00:41:42.582
Please...

00:41:42.626 --> 00:41:46.528
we ask you to return our crew.

00:41:52.302 --> 00:41:54.998
Captain, the photonic lattice
has reappeared.

00:41:55.071 --> 00:41:57.005
Scan it. All sensors.

00:41:57.107 --> 00:41:59.905
I'm reading a massive
particle surge on our holodeck.

00:41:59.943 --> 00:42:02.639
The lattice is gone again.

00:42:02.679 --> 00:42:04.943
Holodeck to Bridge.

00:42:05.048 --> 00:42:06.174
Go ahead, Doctor.

00:42:06.216 --> 00:42:07.376
What is it?

00:42:07.417 --> 00:42:09.317
We have them back, Captain...

00:42:09.352 --> 00:42:11.047
all three of them.

00:42:11.087 --> 00:42:12.782
Good work, Doctor.

00:42:12.822 --> 00:42:14.119
Yeah. Good work.

00:42:14.157 --> 00:42:17.923
Would you mind
telling me where I was?

00:42:17.961 --> 00:42:22.762
Captain's Log, Stardate 48710.5.

00:42:22.799 --> 00:42:24.858
Since the return
of our missing crewmen,

00:42:24.901 --> 00:42:26.163
we've been unable to locate

00:42:26.202 --> 00:42:29.228
any further traces
of the photonic aliens.

00:42:29.272 --> 00:42:30.296
I don't know if the being

00:42:30.340 --> 00:42:33.832
understood language
or just my behavior.

00:42:33.877 --> 00:42:36.402
It would have been
interesting to pursue

00:42:36.446 --> 00:42:37.936
the relationship further.

00:42:37.981 --> 00:42:40.745
It's one of the most exciting
aspects of space exploration...

00:42:40.784 --> 00:42:44.276
meeting new species,
establishing communication,

00:42:44.321 --> 00:42:47.119
sharing differences
and similarities.

00:42:47.157 --> 00:42:49.352
I'm sorry none of that
happened this time.

00:42:49.392 --> 00:42:51.087
But it did.

00:42:51.127 --> 00:42:53.994
It just didn't happen
in very predictable ways.

00:42:54.064 --> 00:42:56.658
But if you think about it,

00:42:56.700 --> 00:43:00.101
we entered into conflict,
communicated,

00:43:00.136 --> 00:43:03.435
and eventually established
a peace treaty with them.

00:43:06.409 --> 00:43:09.674
I'm placing a special
commendation in the logs.

00:43:09.713 --> 00:43:12.944
For exemplary performance
by the Chief Medical Officer

00:43:13.049 --> 00:43:15.540
during his first away mission.

00:43:19.823 --> 00:43:21.120
Thank you.

00:43:21.157 --> 00:43:23.751
I'd like to cite you by name.

00:43:23.793 --> 00:43:26.227
Kes tells me you've chosen one.

00:43:26.262 --> 00:43:27.695
Is that true?

00:43:27.731 --> 00:43:29.164
I had...

00:43:29.199 --> 00:43:31.429
but I'm not sure
I want to keep it.

00:43:31.468 --> 00:43:34.062
The last time I heard
that name spoken

00:43:34.104 --> 00:43:36.800
was a... painful one.

00:43:36.840 --> 00:43:38.967
I don't think
I want to be reminded.

00:43:39.042 --> 00:43:40.839
Sounds like you had
quite an adventure

00:43:40.877 --> 00:43:43.277
on that holodeck, Doctor.

00:43:43.313 --> 00:43:45.941
Yes, I would say so.

00:43:46.983 --> 00:43:48.610
Well...

00:43:48.651 --> 00:43:53.782
something tells me
you haven't had your last one.

00:43:59.429 --> 00:44:01.954
Something tells me
the same thing.
